    {
      "element_kind": "section",
      "id": "s6",
      "role": "model",
      "objective_ids": [
        "o1"
      ],
      "title": "Register and domain also matter",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "kind": "paragraph",
          "spans": [
            {
              "kind": "text",
              "value": "Some collocations belong to a more formal domain. A municipality may fatte en beslutning, a researcher may foreta en vurdering, and a newspaper may report kraftig kritikk. In everyday speech, simpler pairings such as ta en beslutning and gjøre en vurdering can be more natural."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "kind": "example",
          "no": [
            {
              "kind": "text",
              "value": "Utvalget foretok en grundig vurdering før det fattet en beslutning."
            }
          ],
          "en": [
            {
              "kind": "text",
              "value": "The committee carried out a thorough assessment before it made a decision."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "element_kind": "section",
      "id": "s7",
      "role": "model",
      "objective_ids": [
        "o1"
      ],
      "title": "Preposition-bound pairings",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "kind": "paragraph",
          "spans": [
            {
              "kind": "text",
              "value": "Some adjectives and expressions also prefer a particular preposition. These are collocations too: interessert i, avhengig av, enig i, enig med, enig om, and flink til å. Translate the whole pairing, not only the adjective."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "kind": "example",
          "no": [
            {
              "kind": "text",
              "value": "Hun er interessert i språk og flink til å forklare grammatikk."
            }
          ],
          "en": [
            {
              "kind": "text",
              "value": "She is interested in languages and good at explaining grammar."
            }
          ]
        },
